---
title: Plugin trust — from build to LoadFromAssemblyPath
---
%% Verified against the tree on 2026-08-28.
%% The failure mode this exists to make loud: if the manifest and the DLLs disagree,
%% PluginTrustPolicy rejects EVERY plugin and every provider reports "no data" —
%% which reads to a user as a data outage, not as a security refusal.
flowchart TD
    SRC["Plugins/Providers/* · Plugins/Analytics/* · Plugins/Indicators/*"]
    BUILD["Release build of a head<br/>(BlazorClient or WebHost)"]
    TARGET["MSBuild target HashPluginDlls<br/>declared in both csprojs"]
    MAN["plugins_trusted.manifest<br/>one SHA-256 per plugin DLL, written into OutDir"]
    CI["CI: plugin-manifest.yml<br/>uploads it as an artifact; on a v* tag,<br/>attaches it to the GitHub Release"]
    SHIP["Ships next to the app binary"]

    SRC --> BUILD --> TARGET --> MAN
    MAN --> CI --> SHIP

    subgraph BOOT["At load time"]
        PLS["PluginLoaderService.LoadPlugins&lt;T&gt;(dir)"]
        PTP["PluginTrustPolicy<br/>TrustedSha256 set · RequireTrusted flag"]
        HASH["hash the DLL on disk"]
        OK["matches trusted hash — LoadFromAssemblyPath"]
        NO["no match — refuse, log, keep going"]
    end

    SHIP --> PLS
    PLS --> HASH --> PTP
    PTP -->|hash in the set| OK
    PTP -->|hash absent, RequireTrusted true| NO

    subgraph RUN["What a loaded plugin is handed"]
        HTTP["Host HttpClient factory<br/>HostAllowListHandler over<br/>HttpClientHandler AllowAutoRedirect=false"]
        SEC["PluginHostServices.SecureStorage<br/>the only route to a stored key"]
        LOG["IAppLogger — NOT a logger:<br/>this is the error-SPEECH channel a blind user hears"]
    end

    OK --> HTTP & SEC & LOG

    WHEN["When the two disagree:<br/>hand-copying a plugin DLL into a deploy directory,<br/>or an rsync that updates DLLs but not the manifest.<br/>Never copy a plugin DLL by hand — republish."]
    NO --- WHEN

    LAZY["Load timing differs by head:<br/>the hosted terminal loads plugins at boot and logs its trust lines within a second;<br/>the demo loads them lazily on the first chart request, so it logs none until a visitor arrives.<br/>Zero trust lines on the demo minutes after a restart is normal."]
    PLS --- LAZY
